CDNCA proxy_cache_valid with variables.  Original CDNCA change, not
upstream.  With one shared server{} per port (docs/adr/0009, dynamic
routing D8) the cache lifetime of a response must follow the site and the
cache rule chosen at request time; proxy_cache_valid only took a
configuration-time value.  The time argument may now contain variables; it
is evaluated per response with the request's variables (written by Lua in
an earlier phase).  An empty value skips the entry (a later entry for the
status, e.g. "any", applies; none = not cached); "0" means not cached; a
malformed value is logged and means not cached, so a routing failure only
makes a response uncacheable.  Status lists, "any" and the origin's
Cache-Control/Expires/X-Accel-Expires precedence are unchanged; a time
without variables keeps the stock semantics.

